te_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":-0.038809541963567076,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.7900716117498425,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.0049122633500647,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":18.3,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.09959068893772186,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.1,"_gate_pool_share":-0.22061595445585347,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.05099644065961395,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":50.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.026022657497923873,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":12.0,"_gate_margins":-0.0040258255157018304,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":46.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.05075306171889658,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":67.5,"_gate_share_shrink":0.003364533046050777,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":45.8,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0019821605550049554,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":96.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.00696,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":4.6,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Clearway Energy, Inc. operates in the clean energy generation assets business in the United States. It operates through Flexible Generation and Renewables & Storage segments. The company's portfolio comprises approximately 12.9 GW of gross capacity in 27 states, including approximately 10.1 GW of wind, solar, and battery energy storage systems; and approximately 2.8 GW of dispatchable combustion-based power generation assets included in the Flexible Generation segment that provide critical grid reliability services. The company was formerly known as NRG Yield, Inc. and changed its name to Clearway Energy, Inc. in August 2018. Clearway Energy, Inc. was incorporated in 2012 and is based in Princeton, New Jersey. Clearway Energy, Inc. is a subsidiary of Clearway Energy Group LLC.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Craig  Cornelius | CEO, President & Director | Age 45","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Clearway Energy, Inc. is a mid-cap utilities business with a $6.9B market cap on $1.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are contracting by -2.5pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $369M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 26 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.07\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 9.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 212% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Utilities peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -2.5pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 10% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 73% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Reaffirmed Guidance Will Impact Clearway Energy (CWEN) Investors","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/nyse-cwen/clearway-energy/news/how-reaffirmed-guidance-will-impact-clearway-energy-cwen-inv","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794388698.109,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.836,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"How Clearway Energy Inc. Class C (CWEN) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/12/How_Clearway_Energy_Inc._Class_C_CWEN_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_111026035602_1794344162.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794344162.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Clearway Energy, Inc. (NYSE:CWEN) Plans Quarterly Dividend of $0.48","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https: