he EBIT multiple sits 210% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 5.4% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 0.9% (vs the 8% bar).","The 14 covering analysts target $40.14 on average, 20% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 3% falls short of the cost of capital of 6.4%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.79).","It converts 26% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 4.07x.","ROE of 9% is amplified by 8.7x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","It spends 0.2% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 9.6x net debt to EBITDA ($231.0M of cash against $8.3B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 0.4x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 0.53 in the distress zone."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 6.3% over 3 years, 3.6% over 5 years and 5.1% over 10 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 25%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded -2.6% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Margins are contracting (-2.5% trend).","Capex runs only 0.5x depreciation (22.3% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 51, clearing the bar for a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.7%), and institutions hold 89%.","It returns 5.1% a year to shareholders (5.8% in dividends, less 0.7% of net share issuance).","It pays out 212% of earnings, more than it earns, so the dividend is at risk."],"people":["Compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better)."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":44,"head":"Avoid: operating income covers interest only 0.4x.","pros":["Trades 73% below fair value of $124","FCF